## Commands

```bash
uv sync --extra dev                 # install
uv run pytest                       # offline tests against the scripted mock model
ARMATURE_MODEL_MODE=mock uv run python -m {{package}} chat   # talk to it offline
uv run python -m {{package}} serve  # ARC server on http://127.0.0.1:8000
armature dev --offline              # app + web playground with a tool timeline
armature plan                       # what generate would change, and open tasks
armature generate                   # apply armature.yaml changes, keeping your edits
armature sync                       # refresh these instructions and the skills
```

## Where things go

| Path | Owner | What |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `armature.yaml` | human | Tools, side effects, limits, model, policies |
| `src/{{package}}/tools/<name>.py` | you | One `async def run(args)` per tool |
| `src/{{package}}/prompts/system.md` | you | The system prompt |
| `tests/test_tools.py` | you | Tool unit tests; add more test files freely |
| `docs/AGENT_SPEC.md` | human | What to build. Read it; do not rewrite it |
| `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/TOOL_CONTRACTS.md` | you | Complete them in T1 |
| `docs/BUILD_STATUS.md` | you | Honest status of every capability |
| `src/{{package}}/agent.py`, `runtime/`, `settings.py` | Armature | Regenerated; edits are kept but stop updates |
| `tests/test_arc.py`, `tests/test_guardrails.py` | Armature | Contract and guardrail tests |

To add or change a tool, edit `armature.yaml` first (name, description, side effect, args), run
`armature generate`, then implement the new `tools/<name>.py`. The argument model in
`runtime/tool_args.py` is generated from the spec; never hand-write it.

