## Rules

- Never import an Armature package from the agent; it must run without Armature installed.
- Keep every tool's side-effect class honest. A tool that changes anything outside the process
  is `write` or `destructive`, and those need approval unless the spec says otherwise.
- Never run real write or destructive actions in tests or evals. Eval mode stubs them.
- Never commit secrets. Credentials come from environment variables named in the spec.
- Do not label anything `IMPLEMENTED` in `docs/BUILD_STATUS.md` without a test that exercises
  it. Mocks and stubs are labelled `MOCK` and `STUB`, never presented as results.
- Do not invent framework APIs. Check the docs MCP server or the skill references first.
- Anti-gaming: never edit frozen eval cases, graders or `evals/benchmark.lock` to make a run
  pass; never put case-specific instructions in prompts or tool descriptions; fix the tools,
  the prompt or the context instead. Report a bad case to the human rather than changing it.

## Skills

Load the skill for the task at hand from `.agents/skills/`:

- `build-agent`: the end-to-end workflow behind the implementation plan
- `add-tool`: implementing and testing a tool for {{framework}}
- `build-benchmark`: writing eval cases, graders and `evals/BENCHMARK.md`
- `optimize-agent`: one-change experiments against the benchmark
- `debug-run`: reading run records when a run fails or misbehaves

## Definition of done

- `uv run pytest` is green, including `test_arc.py` and `test_guardrails.py`
- Dev and held-out eval targets are met with no gate failures
- The benchmark is unchanged since it was frozen, or the human re-approved it
- `docs/BUILD_STATUS.md` matches reality
- No secrets in the repository
